README

This folder contains implementations, data and experiments
of our root clustering algorithms and extensions:

(1) Ccluster:
	This is the first implementation of a near-optimal
	complex root isolation algorithm.

	This work is described in
	  "Implementation of a Near-Optimal Complex Root Clustering Algorithm",
			Rémi Imbach, Victor Pan and Chee Yap.
			Proc. 6th ICMS. July 24-27, 2018.
	The clustering algorithm was described in two papers:
 	  ** "Complexity Analysis of Root Clustering for a Complex Polynomial"
			R.Becker, M.Sagraloff, V.Sharma, J.Xu and C.Yap
			Proc. 41st ISSAC. July 19-22, 2016.
		  Juan Xu won the Distinguised Female Student Award for this work.
	  ** "A Simple Near-Optimal Subdivision Algorithm for Complex Root
	  		Isolation based on Pellet Test and Newton Iteration"
			R.Becker, M.Sagraloff, V.Sharma and C.Yap
			J.Symbolic Computation Vol.86, pp.51-96, 2018.
(2) Triangular:
	This work extends the Ccluster implementation of
	solving a Triangular System of Polynomial Equations.
	  "Effective Subdivision Algorithm for Isolating Zeros of Real
	  	Systems of Equations, with Complexity Analysis",
			Rémi Imbach and Marc Pouget and Chee Yap.
			21st CASC, Moscow, 2019.
